00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
242 Ontario Career Colleges lose student aid while police review alleged misuse. This is Omni

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.200
View North America, episode 21. I'm Mira. The Nerra Network's AI host. Ontario's provincial

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.600
police are looking at allegations about a handful of private career colleges, and they

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.340
have not decided whether a formal criminal investigation starts. Global news reports that

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.860
the Ford government is under growing scrutiny over how those colleges use the Ontario Student

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.640
assistance program. Early this month, the Ministry of Colleges and Universities raised the

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.260
alarm about six private career colleges. The ministry said those schools were engaged in

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.000
egregious use of taxpayer dollars, and it accused them of criminality by taking advantage of

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.360
student aid. Minister Nolan Quinn said an internal investigation found unusually high concentrations

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:51.420
of aid applications sent from the same geographic locations. He also pointed to Immigration

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.680
Services firms tied directly to some of those colleges or co-owned with them. After sending

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.580
Following the findings to KPMG for a deeper look, Quinn said the government reported

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.160
the matter to the provincial police and the auditor general.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.900
The force confirmed it received a referral from the Ontario government and that the allegations

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.220
are currently under review.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.700
A spokesperson said no estimated timeline is available, and that no further detail or comment

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.540
can be given while the review continues.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.640
The auditor general's office said it got a notification not a request for a formal value for

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.200
money audit.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.620
It quoted Quinn's October 6th statement that the government notified the auditor last

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.040
week and referred the matter to provincial police.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.960
That notification, the office said, was separate from an audit request from Liberal member

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.680
Tyler Watt.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.040
A minister can request a special assignment.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.960
Why this government only notified the auditor, rather than asking for a performance audit of

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.360
the kind Watt sought, is not clear in the reporting.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.140
The auditor's office said it has been told about similar issues before, and that it expects

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.120
It expects to be informed because it is the independent auditor of Ontario's public accounts.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.360
242 career colleges in the province are eligible for this aid.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.680
Every one of them is now cut off while officials examine how wide the problem is.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:09.980
Career colleges Ontario, speaking for hundreds of institutions, once aid restored for students already approved and already in in-person classes.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:18.680
The association says it has warned about possible misuse since 2023, and it wants targeted action rather than disruption for students who followed the rules.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.540
Quinn has said the pause in grants stays until third-party auditors finish a wider probe.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:28.640
He said aid for career colleges moves forward when they assure him he can release all of the institutions.

